# Geometry.Finsler.C11ExactVolume

* **Conditions:** The actual C1,1 translation family with half-Lipschitz displacement and original calibrated clock on the core.
* **Objects:** Exact Haar change of variables for all measurable pieces of its open parameter ball, retaining original calibration and two-sided volume bounds.
* **Proof detail:** Apply the injective Lipschitz area theorem to the same translation, removing Rademacher exceptions and their images internally.

Mathematical sources:
- [D. H. Fremlin, Measure Theory, Volume 2](https://www1.essex.ac.uk/maths/people/fremlin/chap26.pdf#page=26): Theorem 263D(i)–(v), pp. 26–28; Lemma 263C, p. 25; decomposition Lemma 262M, pp. 15–17.
- [D. H. Fremlin, Measure Theory, Volume 2, Chapter 26](https://www1.essex.ac.uk/maths/people/fremlin/chap26.pdf#page=18): Section 262Q, Rademacher theorem and proof, pp. 18–20; Section 262B(c), p. 10 (Lipschitz implies absolutely continuous on bounded intervals).
- [D. H. Fremlin, Measure Theory, Volume 2](https://www1.essex.ac.uk/maths/people/fremlin/chap26.pdf#page=38): Proposition 262D, p. 11; Corollary 262N, p. 17; Proposition 264G, pp. 38–39; Theorem 264I, pp. 40–41.

Source relation (derived): No replacement flow, everywhere derivative or positive population density is assumed.
-/

